# Dryas Workflow (OpenCode)
Process rules for coding sessions on this machine. Full reference: `~/.dryas/docs/dryas-workflow.md` (local notes, if present: `~/.dryas/docs/dryas-local.md`).

## Always
- Brainstorm first: before new work, get the user's approval of a design (`dryas-brainstorm`).
- Multi-step work runs in its own git worktree (`dryas-worktree`); merge after review and verification (`dryas-verify`).
- One agent per worktree: never run two sessions in the same worktree. Parallel loops each get their own worktree and branch.
- Plans are files: `.orchestrate/PLAN.md` in the worktree, sections `## Task N:` with Goal, Scope (globs), Done and Failing test first. Never commit `.orchestrate/`.
- Test first; report only passes you saw.
- Review before merge: spec compliance, then code quality (`/wreview`).
- Commit after review as Conventional Commits; ask before any push.
- Do what was asked, nothing more. Read a file before editing it. Never commit secrets or `.env` files.

## Skills
`/orchestrate` (multi-step tasks), `/wplan` (write a plan), `/wreview` (two-stage review), `/commit` (Jev-gated commit), `/tune` (weekly Jev calibration), `/retro` (lessons from a finished task).
